# ============================================================================
#  zm_qol — .gitignore
#
#  NOTE: the big binaries ARE tracked on purpose. mod.ff, mod.all.sabl/.sabs and
#  deathmachine_zm.all.sabl have no source in this project and cannot be
#  regenerated from anything here — losing them loses the mod. Same for
#  zone_source/base/mod.ff, the donor fastfile every rebuild links from.
#  A checkpoint you can't actually restore from isn't a checkpoint.
# ============================================================================

# Runtime logs pulled off the game — noise, and regenerated every crash hunt.
crashlogs/

# Linker scratch output; build_ff.bat deletes it, but not if a build failed.
zone_out/
zone_source/_regen/

# Staged copies of the .csc sources, written by build_ff.bat step "Staging current
# .csc sources" so the Linker picks them up instead of the donor's stale originals.
# Pure build artifacts — the real files are scripts/zm/**/*.csc.
zone_assets/scripts/

# Ad-hoc backups made before risky edits.
*.bak-*
*.bak

# Replacement stock soundbanks (Carbon BO2 Sound Remaster), deployed by
# build.bat's %OPTFILES% but NOT tracked: cmn_root.all.sabl is 267 MB, well over
# GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit, and unlike mod.all.sabl it is not ours and
# is re-downloadable. A clone without it builds fine and plays stock weapon audio.
# Source: H:\Claude\Carbon Black Ops 2 Sound Remaster\
cmn_root.all.sabl
cmn_root.all.sabs

# Windows/editor cruft
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp

# Sound Studio working copies. The real banks (mod.all.sabl/.sabs,
# deathmachine_zm.all.sabl) ARE tracked - these are scratch duplicates made
# before an alias import and would just bloat history.
*- Copy.sab*
* - Copy.*

# Sound-bank build inputs, regenerated by build_ff.bat from zone_source\base\.
# The donor's 249 payloads and its 1,691-row alias table both come straight back
# out of base\mod.ff + base\mod.all.sabl, so they are derived, not source.
# What IS source: soundbank\mod.all.aliases.additions.csv and sound\.
zone_assets/soundbank/
zone_assets/sound/

# mod.iwd is no longer tracked. Since the upscaled texture pack landed it is
# ~2.1 GB, and git would store a fresh copy of it on every release commit -
# the repo would pass GitHub's file-size limit within one release. It is a
# BUILD OUTPUT and fully reproducible: build.bat regenerates it from the raw
# folders (images/, scripts/, maps/, weapons/, ui_mp/, ...), all of which ARE
# tracked. Nothing is lost that cannot be rebuilt.
#
# 🛑 The other five shipped files stay tracked on purpose - mod.ff,
# mod.all.sabl, mod.all.sabs and deathmachine_zm.all.sabl have no source in
# this project and CANNOT be regenerated. See CLAUDE.md section 5.
mod.iwd

# The upscaled / BO3-style texture pack (2,852 .iwi, ~2.1 GB) that ships inside
# mod.iwd. NOT tracked: it would add 2.1 GB to a repo that is otherwise ~86 MB,
# and it is not this project's work - the master copy is
#   H:\Claude\Projects Sources\add textures to mod
#
# 🛑 This rule does NOT untrack the mod's own 64 images. gitignore never affects
# files git already tracks, and those 64 were committed long before the pack
# arrived, so they stay in history. Only the new bulk textures are skipped.
#
# 🛑 CONSEQUENCE, so nobody is surprised: a FRESH CLONE cannot rebuild the full
# mod.iwd. It will build fine and play fine, just with stock-resolution textures
# until the pack folder above is copied back into images\.
images/*.iwi
